/-!
# An explicit basis for the glued quaternion lattice

The columns of `basisMatrix` define a rank-24 rational lattice. The basis
was obtained from six Hurwitz coordinates by adjoining the conjugates of
`MatrixData.modularRows`, divided on the right by `1+i`. The integer tables
also specify the inverse basis and both matrix generators in that basis.
`Realization.Lattice` checks the identities and proves integral invariance.
No identification with the retained Leech carrier is asserted by these tables.

Source for the six-dimensional matrices: John Bray, ATLAS `6L34G1-Ar6aB0`.
The basis and coordinate certificates are derived here from those matrices;
`Scratch/LeechBlockRealization/generate_data.py` preserves their derivation.
-/

